From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Sync to Exact Content Framerate: timed with vsync off

With Sync to Exact Content Framerate, the runloop's timer paces every
frame, and a context that times its presents (0014, 0018) shows each one
at its own time. Vsync off then has nothing left to switch off: it only
made video presents non-blocking, which shows a frame whenever it happens
to be ready. On a variable refresh panel that is a refresh of that
length, below the panel's range for a 60 Hz game. Video now stays
blocking under Sync to Exact Content Framerate, at init and when the
nonblock state is applied. Fast-forward still presents without blocking.

Measured on SM8550 (Retroid Pocket Nova), VRR on: Super Mario World,
vsync off, 3606 refreshes for 1803 frames in 30 s, none longer than
8.42 ms.

Signed-off-by: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
---
diff --git a/gfx/video_driver.c b/gfx/video_driver.c
--- a/gfx/video_driver.c
+++ b/gfx/video_driver.c
@@ -5680,7 +5680,14 @@
    video.height                      = height;
    video.fullscreen                  = settings->bools.video_fullscreen
          || ((uint32_t)retro_atomic_load_relaxed_int(&video_st->flags) & VIDEO_FLAG_FORCE_FULLSCREEN);
-   video.vsync                       = settings->bools.video_vsync
+   /* With Sync to Exact Content Framerate the runloop's timer paces
+    * every frame, and a context that times its presents shows each at
+    * its own time: vsync off has nothing left to switch off. Presenting
+    * without blocking would only show a frame whenever it happened to be
+    * ready, which on a variable refresh display is a refresh that long.
+    * Fast-forward still presents without blocking. */
+   video.vsync                       = (settings->bools.video_vsync
+            || settings->bools.vrr_runloop_enable)
          && !settings->bools.video_scanline_sync
          && (!(runloop_st->flags & RUNLOOP_FLAG_FORCE_NONBLOCK));
    video.force_aspect                = settings->bools.video_force_aspect;
diff --git a/retroarch.c b/retroarch.c
--- a/retroarch.c
+++ b/retroarch.c
@@ -1578,7 +1578,10 @@
       if (video_st->current_video->set_nonblock_state)
       {
          bool video_nonblock        = enable;
-         if (!video_vsync || runloop_force_nonblock)
+         /* Not with Sync to Exact Content Framerate: see video.vsync in
+          * video_driver_init_internal(). */
+         if (     (!video_vsync && !settings->bools.vrr_runloop_enable)
+               || runloop_force_nonblock)
             video_nonblock = true;
          video_st->current_video->set_nonblock_state(video_st->data,
                video_nonblock,
